1
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:07,100
足迹图课程，第11单元，主动性驱动。
The Footprint course, unit 11, the initiative drive.

2
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:14,300
今天是30天挑战的第19天。接下来的内容，我们将聚焦‘刻意练习’的艺术。
This is challenge day 19 of 30. In the following slide, we’re going to focus on the art of deliberate practice.

4
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:20,960
为什么练习对高绩效至关重要，以及你该如何作为交易员进行练习。
Why practice is imperative to high performance, and how you can practice as a trader.

6
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:52,240
今天我们要讨论的，就是‘刻意练习’这个理念。
What we’re going to talk about today is this idea of deliberate practice.

8
00:00:52,380 --> 00:00:53,902
我会先解释‘刻意’的含义，
I’m going to explain what deliberate means,

9
00:00:53,902 --> 00:00:57,897
然后给你们几个建议，让你们的练习更刻意。
and then I’m going to give you a few ideas of how you can be more deliberate in your practice.

11
00:00:57,900 --> 00:01:04,040
首先，‘刻意’的定义是：有意识且有目的地去做。
So, the first thing: the definition of *deliberate* is it’s done conscientiously and intentionally.

13
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:10,753
现在，把‘有意识’和‘有目的’这两个词写在纸上。
Now, somewhere write down on a piece of paper: *conscientiously* and *intentionally*.

14
00:01:10,753 --> 00:01:15,339
然后问问自己，这一周里，问问自己：
And ask yourself, as you go through the week, ask yourself:

15
00:01:15,339 --> 00:01:22,426
当你观察市场，当你观察图表，当你为一天做准备时，
when you look at something, when you observe the markets, when you’re preparing for your day,

16
00:01:22,426 --> 00:01:29,096
当你记录交易信号时，你是不是有意识且有目的地去做，带着明确目标？
when you’re recording your trade setups, are you doing this conscientiously and intentionally, with purpose?

20
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:33,560
我认为，你们中很多人会发现，实际上自己并没有。
I think what many of you will find is you actually don’t.

22
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:36,912
你们会发现，很多人只是看看图表，
What you’ll find is that many of you do it more as if your charts

23
00:01:36,912 --> 00:01:38,685
然后随手画几条线。
and then put in a line or two here.

24
00:01:38,686 --> 00:01:41,839
然后觉得，‘我付出了一点努力，该得到点回报了。’
Then you feel like, 'I’ve done a bit of effort, I’m deserving of something.'

26
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:46,240
定义的第二部分是：长期且仔细地思考。
Now, the second part of the definition is to engage in long and careful consideration.

28
00:01:50,660 --> 00:01:52,246
这又回到这个问题：
Again, it brings you back to this idea:

29
00:01:52,246 --> 00:01:53,436
很多人看图表时，
when many people look at charts,

30
00:01:53,436 --> 00:01:55,022
只是想，‘市场下跌了，碰到了支撑或某条均线。’
they look at it in the sense of,

31
00:01:58,932 --> 00:02:00,679
但你们中有多少人，真的去思考，首先，
'Well, the market came down, it hit the support or it hit this moving average.'

32
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:05,807
是什么原因让市场跌到那个点的？
But how many of you actually think about, firstly,

33
00:02:05,807 --> 00:02:08,883
是什么让市场最初跌到那个点的
what brought the market down to that point in the first place,

34
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:15,600
你们中很多人可能认为，价格下跌是因为卖家在抛售。
Now, a lot of you might think that price is going down and reflects sellers selling.

36
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:20,260
但按定义，这是错误的。价格下跌可能有很多原因。
That’s, by definition, incorrect. Prices can go down for a number of reasons.

37
00:02:20,340 --> 00:02:24,876
可能是对冲，可能是套利，可能是多头平仓。
There could be hedging reasons, there could be spreading reasons, there could be long liquidation.

40
00:02:24,876 --> 00:02:27,900
价格下跌的原因有很多。
There are a number of reasons why prices go down.

41
00:02:37,383 --> 00:02:39,935
我给你们看那个视频的原因是，
and the reason I’ve shown you that video is,

42
00:02:39,935 --> 00:02:43,252
我们很多人，包括我自己，都很崇拜世界顶尖的高尔夫球手，
a lot of us, including myself, admire the best golfers in the world

43
00:02:43,252 --> 00:02:47,335
和世界顶尖的运动员，我们崇拜他们的技艺和天赋。
and the best athletes in the world, and we admire the skill and talent they have.

46
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:51,427
我们看他们，羡慕他们，心想，‘我也想成为那样的人。’
We look at them, and we envy them, and we think, *‘Well, I wish I could be that person.

48
00:02:51,427 --> 00:02:52,717
‘为什么我不能像他一样？’
Why am I not that person?’*

49
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,247
我来告诉你为什么你做不到：
Well, I’ll tell you why you’re not that person:

50
00:02:55,247 --> 00:02:57,698
因为说到底，你没有进行‘刻意练习’
because, at the end of the day, you do not deliberately practice

51
00:02:57,698 --> 00:02:59,536
每一天都去变得更好一点。
every single day to become that little bit better.

53
00:03:00,380 --> 00:03:03,060
对吧？别忘了，这些专业人士——
Right? Don’t forget, these professionals—

54
00:03:03,060 --> 00:03:04,920
我们只看到冰山一角。
we only see the tip of the iceberg.

55
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:06,580
我们只看到最终结果。
We only see the end outcome.

56
00:03:06,740 --> 00:03:11,660
我们看不到背后数小时的痛苦、挣扎和刻意练习。
We don’t see the hours upon hours of pain, suffering, and purposeful practice that goes into it.

58
00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:19,200
现在，我给你们看的这张图，标注了职业高尔夫球手必须做的事。
Now, the image I’ve shown you has a very simple annotation of what professional golfers have to do.

61
00:03:20,120 --> 00:03:23,940
看这张图，你会发现，
If you look at this picture, you will find that

62
00:03:23,940 --> 00:03:28,524
有时候职业高尔夫球手必须站在3、4或5英尺的推杆前
sometimes a professional golfer has to stand over a 3-, 4-, or 5-foot putt

63
00:03:28,524 --> 00:03:35,018
他必须反复练习同一个推杆，一百遍，不管喜不喜欢。
He has to hit the same putt a hundred times over, whether he likes it or not.

66
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:42,760
为什么？因为这种‘刻意练习’会让他和冠军、和其他人拉开差距
Why? Because this deliberate practice is what will differentiate him from the winner and everyone else

69
00:03:42,760 --> 00:03:44,550
在关键的压力推杆时。
when it comes to that pressure putt.

70
00:03:44,550 --> 00:03:46,340
这就是他们反复练习的原因。
That is why they practice these things,

71
00:03:49,260 --> 00:03:50,500
那么，我们来看几个要点。
So, let's go over a few points.

72
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:57,260
首先，可能有点老生常谈，但练习确实能出真知。
Firstly, it might be a bit cliché, but practice does make perfect. If you practice the same thing

74
00:03:57,260 --> 00:04:02,460
如果你反复练习同一件事，真正执行时，你会做得更好。
time and time again, when it comes to actually delivering, you are going to execute far better.

77
00:04:02,760 --> 00:04:04,832
而你做得更好，并不是因为你练习了。
And you are not going to execute better simply because you practice.

78
00:04:04,832 --> 00:04:07,940
而是因为你对自己做的事更有信心。
You are going to execute better because there is a lot more trust in what you are doing.

81
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:11,859
我们进行‘刻意练习’是为了培养真正的技能。
We deliberately practice because we want to develop real skill.

82
00:04:11,859 --> 00:04:15,471
天天交易市场，并不是为了找到那些位置，
Trading the markets day in, day out is not about finding those levels,

83
00:04:15,471 --> 00:04:18,249
点一下，赚点钱，然后走人，
clicking, and then making a bit of money, moving on,

84
00:04:18,249 --> 00:04:19,916
第二天再来。
and coming back the next day.

85
00:04:19,980 --> 00:04:23,580
那不是交易。交易是培养核心技能。
That is not trading. Trading is about developing key skill sets.

86
00:04:23,760 --> 00:04:28,375
无论是学习管理价格，还是提升风险管理能力，
Whether that is learning to manage prices, becoming better at managing risk,

87
00:04:28,375 --> 00:04:33,374
更好地交易多种市场，还是理解差异——
better at trading an array of markets, whether that is understanding the difference

88
00:04:33,374 --> 00:04:39,912
算法交易还是长期波段交易，每一样都是独立的技能。
between algorithmic trading or longer-term swing trading, Each one of these is a skill in its own.

90
00:04:39,914 --> 00:04:42,606
而为了培养这些技能，
And in order to develop those skills,

91
00:04:42,606 --> 00:04:48,375
你必须进行‘刻意练习’来提升那项技能。
you have to deliberately practice what is going to make you better at that skill.

94
00:04:48,880 --> 00:04:50,900
我们已经聊过冰山一角了。
We have already spoken about the tip of the iceberg.

95
00:04:51,320 --> 00:04:53,702
别忘了，最终结果只是冰山一角。
Don’t forget, the end outcome is just the tip.

96
00:04:53,702 --> 00:04:57,511
你会羡慕一些交易员，我也会看看身边的交易员，然后想，
You can marvel at some traders, and I can look at traders around me and think,

97
00:04:57,511 --> 00:05:00,606
‘哇，这些家伙一天赚十万镑，’
'Oh wow, these guys, they are making a hundred thousand pounds a day,'

98
00:05:00,606 --> 00:05:02,510
‘哇，为什么我不是那样的人？’
and, 'Wow, why am I not that person?'

99
00:05:02,514 --> 00:05:04,657
为什么我不能像他一样？
Why can’t I be as good as him?

100
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:08,220
但白天我看不到幕后发生了什么。
But in the day, I don’t get to see what goes on behind the scenes.

102
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:11,560
我不知道他周末承受了什么压力。
I don’t know what sort of pressure or things he does on the weekend.

104
00:05:11,780 --> 00:05:16,620
我不知道这个家伙每天花几小时做什么心理训练。
I don’t know what sort of mental exercises this guy is spending hours every single day doing.

106
00:05:17,260 --> 00:05:18,900
对吧？但他肯定在做些什么。
Right? But he’s doing *something*.

107
00:05:19,700 --> 00:05:21,374
这才是关键。
And that’s the important thing.

108
00:05:21,374 --> 00:05:24,722
他在刻意练习某些能让他更优秀的东西。
He’s deliberately practicing something that makes him that little bit better.

109
00:05:24,722 --> 00:05:25,559
那捷径呢？对吧？
Then, shortcuts. Right?

110
00:05:29,309 --> 00:05:31,719
捷径？没有捷径这回事。
Shortcuts. There is no such thing as a shortcut.

112
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:34,440
我无法教会你们中的任何人交易。
I cannot teach any one of you to trade.

113
00:05:34,780 --> 00:05:36,620
没人能教会你们中的任何人交易。
No one can teach any one of you to trade.

114
00:05:36,780 --> 00:05:38,800
没有书。没有导师。
There is no book. There is no mentor.

115
00:05:39,020 --> 00:05:40,520
没有课程。没有工具。
There is no program. No tool.

116
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:46,080
这个世界上没有任何东西能给你交易成功的捷径。什么都没有。对吧？
There’s nothing in this world that can give you a shortcut to trading success. Nothing. All right?

118
00:05:46,740 --> 00:05:48,100
这是你首先要理解的。
That’s the first thing to understand.

119
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:52,660
只有你，通过刻意练习，才能在长期中培养出捷径。
Only you, through deliberate practice, can develop the shortcuts over the long run.

121
00:05:53,440 --> 00:05:57,260
这才是关键。交易一点都不有趣，伙计们，我发誓。
That's the important thing to understand. Trading isn't fun, guys, I promise you.

122
00:05:57,460 --> 00:06:00,040
交易简直太可怕了。好吧？
Trading is absolutely horrible. Okay?

123
00:06:00,200 --> 00:06:01,088
它不应该...
It shouldn't be...

124
00:06:01,088 --> 00:06:04,642
我超爱这个游戏，但有时候真的很讨厌它。
I love this game to bits, but I absolutely hate it sometimes.

125
00:06:06,460 --> 00:06:08,240
如果交易有趣，那你肯定做错了。
If it's fun, you're not doing the right thing.

126
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:11,760
这是份枯燥的工作。和其他工作一样是个流程。
It's a boring job. It's a process like any job.

127
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:15,000
一天结束时，我们盈利了，我们开心。对吧？
We get to the end of the day, we're green, we're happy. Okay?

128
00:06:15,060 --> 00:06:18,305
因为我们遵循了流程，刻意做了该做的事，
Because we followed the process, we deliberately did what we needed to do,

129
00:06:18,305 --> 00:06:20,301
最终结果是积极的。对吧？
and the end outcome was positive. All right?

130
00:06:20,302 --> 00:06:21,799
白天交易的时候，一点都不有趣。
During the day, it's not fun.

131
00:06:21,940 --> 00:06:23,638
坐在这里两三个小时，
It's not fun sitting here for two, three hours,

132
00:06:23,638 --> 00:06:26,657
无聊得要命，因为市场什么都没给你。
and you're bored out of your head waiting, because the market is not giving you anything.

134
00:06:27,420 --> 00:06:30,740
这一点很重要。接下来是‘刻意练习’。对吧？
Important to understand that. Then, deliberate practice. All right?

135
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:35,140
高尔夫球手不会去练习场打一千个球就算了。对吧？
Golfers don't just go out onto a driving range and hit a thousand balls. All right?

137
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:37,000
他们会针对非常具体的技能训练。
They work on very specific skills.

138
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:39,640
他们会针对游戏中非常具体的环节训练。
They work on very specific elements of the game.

139
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:42,760
你有在针对交易中具体的技能集训练吗？
Are you working on specific sets of your trading game?

140
00:06:43,160 --> 00:06:45,030
如果你想成为专业交易员，
If you want to be a professional trader,

141
00:06:45,030 --> 00:06:48,536
那你凭什么比其他想成为专业交易员的人强？
what makes you any different from anyone else who wants to be a professional trader?

143
00:06:50,220 --> 00:06:53,860
然后是工具。用于‘刻意练习’的工具有哪些？
Then, tools. What are some of the tools you can use for deliberate practice?

145
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:56,740
好的。首先，导师是其中之一。
Well, yes. First and foremost, a mentor is one of them.

147
00:06:56,900 --> 00:06:59,020
你需要有人指导你。对吧？
You need someone to guide you. Right?

148
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:01,140
今天你们在听这个课程，
You're listening in on this today, guys.

149
00:07:01,400 --> 00:07:03,460
已经朝正确方向迈出了一步。
Already, you are taking a step in the right direction.

150
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:05,960
为什么？因为我可能经验更丰富，
Why? Well, because I've probably got more experience,

151
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,340
或者说我比你们大多数人领先。
Or I'm ahead of most of you.

152
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:11,140
换句话说，我经历过你们可能会遇到的坑。
In other words, I've been through some of the pitfalls that some of you are going to go through.

154
00:07:11,640 --> 00:07:14,840
所以，我指导你们，给你们提个醒——‘哎，你知道吗？’
So, me guiding you, me giving you a little heads-up—like, 'Oh, you know what?'

155
00:07:14,900 --> 00:07:17,120
你可能某天会爆仓。对吧？
You're probably going to blow out at some point. Right?

156
00:07:17,320 --> 00:07:18,484
我给你提个醒，
Me giving you a heads-up,

157
00:07:18,484 --> 00:07:20,579
你可能某天会平均一个坏交易，
you're probably going to average a bad trade sometime

158
00:07:20,579 --> 00:07:22,674
然后得学一个非常非常宝贵的教训。
and have to learn a very, very valuable lesson.

159
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:27,156
这会加快你的学习曲线。
is going to speed your learning curve up.

160
00:07:27,156 --> 00:07:31,716
这才是关键，这就是你需要导师的原因。
And that's what's important, and that's why you want a mentor.

161
00:07:33,140 --> 00:07:34,700
你们必须积极交易。
You have to be active traders.

162
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:37,419
如果你坐在那里盯着市场，想着，
If you're sitting and looking at these markets, thinking,

163
00:07:37,419 --> 00:07:39,331
‘唉，今天只做了一笔交易，因为’
'Well, I took one trade today because,'

164
00:07:39,331 --> 00:07:41,243
‘我找不到其他入场形态了。’
'I couldn’t find any other setups.'

165
00:07:43,380 --> 00:07:44,520
这可不够，伙计们。
That’s not good enough, guys.

166
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:50,760
你必须不断搜索市场中的机会。新的机会。
You have to be constantly scouring the market for opportunity. For *new* opportunity. Not just those opportunities,

168
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:56,760
不是那些教科书里的针柱线、支撑阻力线。对吧？重要通知：
those pin bars and those support and resistance lines you learned in the textbook. Okay? Newsflash:

170
00:07:56,900 --> 00:08:00,840
如果在教科书里，人人都有。对吧？如果在书里，
If it’s in a textbook, everyone’s got it. All right? If it’s in a book

171
00:08:00,840 --> 00:08:06,700
或者有个演讲者给你一堆所谓的好信号，重要通知：人人都有。
or if there’s this wonderful speaker giving you all these wonderful setups, well, newsflash: everyone’s got it.

174
00:08:06,740 --> 00:08:12,420
这是公开信息。你必须每天都保持主动，
It’s public information. You have to be active every single day because when you’re active,

175
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:16,680
因为主动时，你会学会开发、记忆、发现新策略。
you will learn to develop, memorize, and see new strategies.

176
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:21,060
这才是最终让你抓住真正机会的关键。聪明的分析。
That’s what will give you a real opportunity at the end of the day. Smart analysis.

178
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:24,620
别花三四小时盯着市场。你在浪费时间。
Don’t spend three or four hours scouring the markets. You’re wasting your time.

179
00:08:25,340 --> 00:08:29,880
要聪明地看市场。别用七种不同工具。
Be smart in how you view the market. Don’t have seven different tools.

180
00:08:30,140 --> 00:08:32,100
别用七种不同指标。
Don’t have seven different indicators.

181
00:08:32,400 --> 00:08:35,000
你只是把简单的过程复杂化了。
You're just complicating a simple process.

182
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:36,300
坚持用一种。
Stick to one.

183
00:08:36,860 --> 00:08:41,700
保持简单。保持聪明。用非常明确的目的分析市场。
Keep it simple. Keep it smart. Analyze the market with a very specific intent.

185
00:08:42,180 --> 00:08:47,180
这样，你会得到非常明确的结果。然后，回放功能。
That way, you're going to get very specific outcomes. Then, replay functionality.

187
00:08:47,700 --> 00:08:50,622
有多少人——我等会给你们演示——
How often—and I'm going to show you this in a minute—

188
00:08:50,622 --> 00:08:52,326
有多少人真正用过回放功能，
how many of you actually ever replay

